LAST_SUCCESS=Phase 3 core DONE (real identity keys) + handset UI revamp, built + deployed (safe, backed up /state). wart-call: random per-call ICE ufrag/pwd (random_ice_cred) replacing fixed ufrAgentA/B; 14/14 signal tests pass. engine: call.rs + engine.rs now use REAL serialized identity public keys for the SRTP HKDF (my_identity=store.identity().identity_key().serialize(); peer via store.get_identity(ServiceId.to_protocol_address(dev1)); self-call keys with my_identity). identity_for(ACI) removed. UI: handset is now ONE big 128px toggle in the thread header — GREEN=place / RED=hang up (no separate End button); CallBar shows status + big Accept(📞)/Decline(📵) only for incoming. Builds (6.0M), deployed.
NOTES=UNVERIFIED LIVE: the green->red->end toggle (my adb taps on the TOP HEADER strip don't register — back button taps fail too; tall header may have a status-bar touch-inset issue worth checking — ASK USER to finger-test the big green handset: tap=place(red), tap red=end(green)). Bigger-handset SIZE fix visually confirmed. Real-Signal interop (audio with a real Signal client) STILL untested — needs the user's real Signal app + iteration (RTP ext ids, DTLS-vs-DH-only, multi-ring). Also unverified: duplex audio MMAP -889, NAT/TURN. Carry-over: no call timeout. NEXT: user finger-tests handset; then real-Signal-client interop iteration.
